        "original_id": "7f73526d-e334-5fee-a7df-cd61f110c4c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon\n- Places: France\n- Concepts: mutualist philosophy, federalism\n- Events: French Revolution of 1848\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- After the French Revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and then referred to himself as a federalist.\n- Cercle Proudhon was a political group founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.",
